    {
        "content": "<p>dicej opened <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15325\">PR #15325</a> from <code>dicej:fix-14769</code> to <code>bytecodealliance:main</code>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>This addresses a condition in <code>wasmtime_wasi_http::handler</code> where a worker may accept new requests faster than it can deliver events to existing tasks, leading to starvation and potential resource exhaustion.</p>\n<p>The solution is to check for any ready-to-run work items in <code>Accessor::poll_ready_for_concurrent_call</code> and, if any are found, return <code>Poll::Pending</code>, which directs <code>wasmtime_wasi_http::handler::Worker::run_</code> to return control to the event loop so it can drain the items before taking on new work.</p>\n<p>Fixes #14769<br>\n</p>\n</blockquote>",
